{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither","id":1274765,"title":"Chimerstry illusions : mental or physical ? Or both ? Or neither ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-16T13:36:20-08:00","id":1274765,"title":"Chimerstry illusions : mental or physical ? Or both ? Or neither ?","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I'm running a chronicle where my players' characters will soon run into a Ravnos vampire who uses Chimerstry a lot, and I was wondering how to make it interact with my PCs' powers. Is it a mental illusion - that could be fought with the Mind sphere - or a physical illusion that would be the equivalent of a Forces effect ? Or something else ?<br /> <br /> The problem is that Vampire does not clearly separates physical and mental effects - for example, it is known that you can fight Chimerstry with Auspex, but Auspex is the discipline of true perception, both mental and physical. Chimerstry seems to fundamentally be an art of deception and manipulation, which would suggest mental illusions, but some aspects of it like the fact that it can affect an arbitrary number of people in the same way, or that some effects addresses specific senses, suggests that it creates sensory stimulations.<br /> <br /> My interpretation would be that Chimerstry is a form of &quot;low level&quot; mental illusion; it neither creates physical illusions nor directly manipulates the target's belief about what is there, but instead hacks the target's low level perceptions to make them consistent with the Ravnos' imagined reality and not the real world. I would allow it to be fought with both Mind (because someone is manipulating your perceptions) and some careful applications of other spheres, typically Forces and/or Matter (to notice that what your mundane senses perceive is inconsistent with your magickal perceptions).<br /> <br /> Any thoughts or official position about that? Thanks !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24540-alexendy","name":"alexendy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24540_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T05:07:17-08:00","id":1274863,"title":"","content":"It also has a spiritual component because it's illusions are real in the Dreaming. But that probably isn't relevant to sense them as illusions (altrough understanding it's exact nature could justify a reduction in the difficulty to detect them as such)<br /> <br /> Personally I would go with Mind. My interpretation it's that Chimestry works by befudling reality mixing it with dreams. Mind doesn't cover only the brain, but also things like dreams and symbols understood in a more conceptual fashion (for instance, it can be used to understand the meaning of cyphered text), and thus it should be able to sense the irreality of Chimestry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-17-2018, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T06:15:20-08:00","id":1274876,"title":"","content":"My gaming table have always considered it Mind magick. But that has mostly been when replicating the effects, not combating them.<br /> But i would see a Mind effect that helps the mage to pierce through illusions would be equally valid if the illusions came from a Ravnos as if they came from another mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T13:19:05-08:00","id":1274945,"title":"","content":"I put Chimerstry as a &quot;something else&quot; case. The interpretation I got was two part as it was summoning a chimerical object from the dreaming and temporarily granting people visibility into it. Chimerical creations are powered via glamour aka quintessence so a character could combat it by cutting off the ability to perceive the chimerical with mind, messing with the quintessence flow with prime, or mind plus spirit to try to manipulate the summoned object.<br /> <br /> This may be overcomplicating things, but the interaction with the fae suggested it was more than just raw mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T15:03:46-08:00","id":1275174,"title":"","content":"Its very half assed Pattern spheres. Ravnos bend the Maya to create their effects but because its only the top layer it seems particularly illusionary. But fire they make would be effected by Forces. Matter they make by Matter. Life by life etc. It just lacks depth. So mages are probably the worst thing to throw chimestry at since sensory effects will right away show &quot;oh hey there's soething wrong with that fire&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T08:01:23-08:00","id":1275516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1275174#post1275174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its very half assed Pattern spheres. Ravnos bend the Maya to create their effects but because its only the top layer it seems particularly illusionary. But fire they make would be effected by Forces. Matter they make by Matter. Life by life etc. It just lacks depth. So mages are probably the worst thing to throw chimestry at since sensory effects will right away show &quot;oh hey there's soething wrong with that fire&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I see the tie between Maya and effects being influenced by pattern spheres. Can you elaborate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T16:17:39-08:00","id":1275652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1275516#post1275516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure I see the tie between Maya and effects being influenced by pattern spheres. Can you elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When a Ravnos creates a Chimerical fire they are changing reality on the most superficial level. It lacks greater depth in levels of &quot;Realness&quot;(That is ultimately overcome at level 9). So functionally what they make would be effected as it is the real thing its just not real enough. Its why when you see through Chimestry unlike say Obfuscate it doesn't change things. You just can tell the wall is fake, or the fire isn't real the fire doesn't go away or uncover what is hidden.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T17:41:30-08:00","id":1275672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1275652#post1275652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> When a Ravnos creates a Chimerical fire they are changing reality on the most superficial level. It lacks greater depth in levels of &quot;Realness&quot;(That is ultimately overcome at level 9). So functionally what they make would be effected as it is the real thing its just not real enough. Its why when you see through Chimestry unlike say Obfuscate it doesn't change things. You just can tell the wall is fake, or the fire isn't real the fire doesn't go away or uncover what is hidden.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why does a changeling get burned by Chimerstry fire and others don't, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T21:42:25-08:00","id":1275719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1275672#post1275672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does a changeling get burned by Chimerstry fire and others don't, then?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Presuming they are using the proper level of chimestry to do so. They have chimerical existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T10:57:51-08:00","id":1275849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1275719#post1275719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Presuming they are using the proper level of chimestry to do so. They have chimerical existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ravnos Revised Clanbook indicates that chimerstry hurts fae.<br /> <br /> Also from the Ravnos revised clanbook:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Karavalanisha Vrana describes Chimerstry as a way to warp or twist the surface of maya. Maya is what we call \u201creality.\u201d It\u2019s an illusion that over-lays whatever the \u201creally\u201d real world is. Apparently, it extends through several levels from the purely physical to the purely spiritual (bear with me; I\u2019m not an expert on this stuff). What Chimerstry can do is take something from the realm of pure spirit, or thought, and make it appear in the realm of the physical, or \u201cpure illusion.\u201d Paradoxically, Chimerstry rarely manifests substance, often giving the appearance of tactile presence. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T21:51:23-08:00","id":1276012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1275849#post1275849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Ravnos Revised Clanbook indicates that chimerstry hurts fae.<br /> <br /> Also from the Ravnos revised clanbook:<br /> <br /> &quot;The Karavalanisha Vrana describes Chimerstry as a way to warp or twist the surface of maya. Maya is what we call \u201creality.\u201d It\u2019s an illusion that over-lays whatever the \u201creally\u201d real world is. Apparently, it extends through several levels from the purely physical to the purely spiritual (bear with me; I\u2019m not an expert on this stuff). What Chimerstry can do is take something from the realm of pure spirit, or thought, and make it appear in the realm of the physical, or \u201cpure illusion.\u201d Paradoxically, Chimerstry rarely manifests substance, often giving the appearance of tactile presence. &quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are different levels of Chimestry. if say you used level 1 to make a chimerical bat it only can effect one sense, so it wouldn't hurt a Changeling in my mind. Assuming you are using 3+ though its full and real to them. Because it exists on that level of reality.<br /> <br /> It however lacks full and tangible reality on the layer of existence that is the mundane world. Only having the echos of such. Thus fire may only appear to burn but not cause wounds to another vampire.<br /> <br /> It would also presumably lack existence on the various umbral levels.<br /> <br /> Suffice to say I would let pattern spheres see &quot;that's not really fire&quot; with Forces, or &quot;that's not a real wall&quot; with matter or &quot;that's not a real kitten&quot; with Life. I wouldn't let someone use a &quot;mind barrier&quot; to protect against chimestry(but I would vs obfuscate). That it has Existence on a chimerical level doesn't really matter for purposes of this because its not purely a chimerical effect.<br /> <br /> If it were a pure chimerical effect it wouldn't effect nonenchanted types and it doesn't seem to be &quot;this power temporarily enchants you&quot; its more like a halfassed attempt to call upon the wyrd. In which case once again if a changeling pulls a sword on me and has called upon the wyrd that item is effected by pattern spheres, I can't &quot;mind it&quot; away. Though theoretically there's some sort of Mind/prime/spirit effect that can control banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T10:59:28-08:00","id":1276086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1276012#post1276012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are different levels of Chimestry. if say you used level 1 to make a chimerical bat it only can effect one sense, so it wouldn't hurt a Changeling in my mind. Assuming you are using 3+ though its full and real to them. Because it exists on that level of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem to be the direction this is pointing. Changelings' tie to maya make even low level chimerstry abilities much more substantive in terms of being able to do chimerical damage.<br /> <br /> I do see your point in using the pattern spheres to see through the illusion for non-changelings/chimerical entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-22T13:31:49-08:00","id":1276112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PhillyCuriosity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1276086#post1276086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't seem to be the direction this is pointing. Changelings' tie to maya make even low level chimerstry abilities much more substantive in terms of being able to do chimerical damage.<br /> <br /> I do see your point in using the pattern spheres to see through the illusion for non-changelings/chimerical entities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nothing about Chimestry says its MORE effective on Chimerical reality. Just that it exists on chimerical reality. So if you use a level that only gives one sense there's no reason it should get extra powers ...and fire that is frozen and doesn't burn is a thing that exists in the dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T10:13:35-08:00","id":1277219,"title":"","content":"I treat Chimerstry as substantially Spirit-based, but which can be defended against using Mind (to shield oneself or others from being deceived) <i>or </i>Spirit (to dismantle the thing/stuff on its own terms).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-31T14:34:07-08:00","id":1277709,"title":"","content":"When we get the 5th edition clan writeup, we\u2019ll have an official ruling in the form of how they reinterpret Chimerstry, since unique disciplines are out. My guess is that it\u2019ll be reimagined as one or more Obfuscate amalgam powers with a Fortitude prerequisite. So it\u2019s fundamentally mental manipulation (Obfuscate), but they can lend it a quality of solidity based on their experience using the Blood to solidify their own bodies (Fortitude). That also makes the Ravnos the most likely practitioners, as I don\u2019t think another clan has those disciplines together. <br /> <br /> And Obfuscate, as we know, is fundamentally a matter of subtly telling nearby minds what to perceive (or not perceive), so definitely under the purview of Mind. After all, it\u2019s only an illusion if it\u2019s perceived to be there but in some meaningful sense is actually *not* there. (Yeah, yeah, \u201cthe entire world is an illusion,\u201d etc., etc., but you know what I mean.) Even now, both Chimerstry and Obfuscate are effectively illusion powers; Obfuscate just has a narrower range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 12-31-2018, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-31T15:16:25-08:00","id":1277718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1277709#post1277709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When we get the 5th edition clan writeup, we\u2019ll have an official ruling in the form of how they reinterpret Chimerstry, since unique disciplines are out. My guess is that it\u2019ll be reimagined as one or more Obfuscate amalgam powers with a Fortitude prerequisite. So it\u2019s fundamentally mental manipulation (Obfuscate), but they can lend it a quality of solidity based on their experience using the Blood to solidify their own bodies (Fortitude). That also makes the Ravnos the most likely practitioners, as I don\u2019t think another clan has those disciplines together.<br /> <br /> And Obfuscate, as we know, is fundamentally a matter of subtly telling nearby minds what to perceive (or not perceive), so definitely under the purview of Mind. After all, it\u2019s only an illusion if it\u2019s perceived to be there but in some meaningful sense is actually *not* there. (Yeah, yeah, \u201cthe entire world is an illusion,\u201d etc., etc., but you know what I mean.) Even now, both Chimerstry and Obfuscate are effectively illusion powers; Obfuscate just has a narrower range.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except... Obfuscate can now show up on Film. That's the issue with its all &quot;mental trickery&quot;... unless &quot;everything has a mind&quot; and then its sort of a useless thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-31T15:37:21-08:00","id":1277724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1277718#post1277718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except... Obfuscate can now show up on Film. That's the issue with its all &amp;quot;mental trickery&amp;quot;... unless &amp;quot;everything has a mind&amp;quot; and then its sort of a useless thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is an advanced power that lets you do that. Still an illusion, though; the vampire is still standing there. The real question is whether the vampire is able to fool the camera or is somehow implanting the mental manipulation onto it so that the illusion becomes automated. <br /> <br /> I prefer the latter, and the text sticks with the idea that Obfuscation is a kind of \u201cambient mesmerism,\u201d so I guess what\u2019s happening is the vampire is effectively mesmerizing people through the camera. Also, that\u2019s the creepier option, so it has to be true, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-31T17:45:23-08:00","id":1277735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1277724#post1277724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, there is an advanced power that lets you do that. Still an illusion, though; the vampire is still standing there. The real question is whether the vampire is able to fool the camera or is somehow implanting the mental manipulation onto it so that the illusion becomes automated.<br /> <br /> I prefer the latter, and the text sticks with the idea that Obfuscation is a kind of \u201cambient mesmerism,\u201d so I guess what\u2019s happening is the vampire is effectively mesmerizing people through the camera. Also, that\u2019s the creepier option, so it has to be true, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems pretty tame and safe vs &quot;all reality is just an illusion on some level&quot; especially in a world of subjective reality which is mage..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-31T18:10:06-08:00","id":1277739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1277735#post1277735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems pretty tame and safe vs &amp;quot;all reality is just an illusion on some level&amp;quot; especially in a world of subjective reality which is mage..</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, and I absolutely think the Ravnos themselves would see it in quasi-magelike terms, but then you have to think about vampires edging in on actual Mage territory, gamewise. Even the Tremere don\u2019t just pop things from their imaginations into reality. So I guess vampire disciplines *are* kind of tame compared to awakened magic. Very effective at what they do, but not so much hacking reality as superficial tweaks that exploit flesh and blood and the minds of those who are (or were) made of them. <br /> <br /> But if the Ravnos\u2019s mystical view of things is accurate in your view, then that\u2019s cool. This being the WoD, there probably shouldn\u2019t ever be a *definitive* answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-01T13:11:04-08:00","id":1277907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1274765-chimerstry-illusions-mental-or-physical-or-both-or-neither?p=1277739#post1277739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Granted, and I absolutely think the Ravnos themselves would see it in quasi-magelike terms, but then you have to think about vampires edging in on actual Mage territory, gamewise. Even the Tremere don\u2019t just pop things from their imaginations into reality. So I guess vampire disciplines *are* kind of tame compared to awakened magic. Very effective at what they do, but not so much hacking reality as superficial tweaks that exploit flesh and blood and the minds of those who are (or were) made of them.<br /> <br /> But if the Ravnos\u2019s mystical view of things is accurate in your view, then that\u2019s cool. This being the WoD, there probably shouldn\u2019t ever be a *definitive* answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Before 5e Tremere had Path of Conjuring which let the pop things into reality. Same with Lure of flames.<br /> <br /> What separated chimestry from Obfuscate in pre 5e it it always showed up on Film, now obfuscate eventually started picking up tricks around that, but that might be more an argument that Obfuscate is &quot;Base&quot; Chimestry like Celerity is &quot;base&quot; Temporis. A Changeling could also climb a chimerical ladder and there were combos that would allow the Ravnos to do the same. All of this suggests its not &quot;mental&quot; trickery at all. Just like I can make a character invisible using Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-08T11:52:43-08:00","id":1279524,"title":"","content":"Some further notes from The Book of Lost Dreams <br /> Chimestry<br /> The Discipline of Chimerstry (see Vampire Players Guide) creates illusions that can be perceived by mortals and all Awakened beings. However, these illusions are spawned in the Dreaming and become all the more real to the Kithain. All illusions created by Chimerstry have chimerical reflections as well. These chimera often remain in existence long after the original illusion has faded. For every success earned in creating an illusion with Chimerstry, the chimera will remain for at least an additional day. How this chimera acts depends upon the nature of the illusion that was cast. Inanimate chimera generally remain in the area where they were created, and can be interacted with by changelings just like any other inanimate chimera. These are almost always considered to be Incidental chimera (see Changeling: The Dreaming second edition, pg. 218). Animate chimera can take on a life of their own, often with extremely unpredictable effects. A Kithain can sense the use of Chimerstry within a mile with a simple Kenning roll (difficulty 7). One success gives the Kithain a general idea of where the Discipline is being used, while five successes allows the Kithain to pinpoint the exact location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}